{"generated_at":"2026-09-06T22:07:49+00:00","produced_by":"mgmt_export.py","gate_doc":"docs/IN_GAME_MANAGEMENT_GATE.md","gate_frozen_at":"2026-09-06","gate_verdict":"DESCRIPTIVE ONLY. The season-controlled split-half correlation of 0.0691 sits INSIDE its permutation null band [-0.1504, 0.1243], so per-agent decision value in the running game is not a repeatable property of the agent. The board may render and be sorted by attempt VOLUME, which is a style axis; the plus metric is WITHHELD, exactly as leverage_board does today.","headline":{"league_steals_second_at":0.75,"against_a_breakeven_of":0.7503,"sum_dv_wins_second":-0.19,"sum_dv_wins_third":4.31,"sum_dv_wins_home":-2.33,"net_dv_all_seasons_wins":1.79,"redistributable_pool_abs_dv_wins":30.96,"games":19130,"sentence":"Across eight seasons the league steals second almost exactly as often as it should. Steals of third pay, steals of home do not, and the whole running game is worth about one and a half wins to the entire league."},"running_game":{"n_attempts_priced":13971,"by_target":{"2B":{"n":11977,"success_rate":0.75,"mean_breakeven_p":0.7534,"median_breakeven_p":0.7429,"share_of_attempts_below_their_own_breakeven":0.5718,"swing_weighted_breakeven_p":0.7503,"mean_dv":-1.5e-05,"sum_dv_wins":-0.19,"mean_er":-3.6e-05,"sum_er_wins":-0.43,"mean_swing_on_success":0.05313,"mean_swing_on_failure":0.05332,"swing_ratio_failure_over_success":1.0035},"3B":{"n":1932,"success_rate":0.7614,"mean_breakeven_p":0.7309,"median_breakeven_p":0.732,"share_of_attempts_below_their_own_breakeven":0.6749,"swing_weighted_breakeven_p":0.7284,"mean_dv":0.00223,"sum_dv_wins":4.31,"mean_er":-0.000636,"sum_er_wins":-1.23,"mean_swing_on_success":0.06603,"mean_swing_on_failure":0.0694,"swing_ratio_failure_over_success":1.051},"HOME":{"n":62,"success_rate":0.2581,"mean_breakeven_p":0.5865,"median_breakeven_p":0.5887,"share_of_attempts_below_their_own_breakeven":0.0484,"swing_weighted_breakeven_p":0.5584,"mean_dv":-0.037595,"sum_dv_wins":-2.33,"mean_er":-0.010115,"sum_er_wins":-0.63,"mean_swing_on_success":0.09337,"mean_swing_on_failure":0.14083,"swing_ratio_failure_over_success":1.5083}},"by_season":{"2018":{"n":1606,"success_rate":0.703,"sum_dv_wins":-3.65,"sum_er_wins":-1.73},"2019":{"n":1399,"success_rate":0.7041,"sum_dv_wins":-3.28,"sum_er_wins":-1.09},"2021":{"n":1354,"success_rate":0.729,"sum_dv_wins":-1.35,"sum_er_wins":-0.13},"2022":{"n":1522,"success_rate":0.7523,"sum_dv_wins":0.3,"sum_er_wins":-0.58},"2023":{"n":2080,"success_rate":0.7841,"sum_dv_wins":4.51,"sum_er_wins":0.65},"2024":{"n":2081,"success_rate":0.7708,"sum_dv_wins":2.56,"sum_er_wins":-0.68},"2025":{"n":2122,"success_rate":0.7644,"sum_dv_wins":2.1,"sum_er_wins":0.71},"2026":{"n":1807,"success_rate":0.7565,"sum_dv_wins":0.6,"sum_er_wins":0.57}},"excluded":{"prior_state_change":348,"origin_base_empty":17,"two_outs_crosses_the_boundary":9328,"unpriceable_state":0},"decomposition":{"dv":"the DECISION, priced with the league-average success rate for that season and target base. Was sending anybody here a good idea?","er":"the EXECUTION RESIDUAL, realized minus expected. Did this runner beat the throw? Attributed to the runner, never to the manager.","identity":"DV + ER = the realized win-probability change, exactly","identity_max_abs_error":0.0},"why_two_out_attempts_are_excluded":"with nobody out or one out a caught stealing leaves the inning alive, so both sides of the comparison come from the same monotone model. With two out it ends the inning, so the alternative comes from the measured half-inning-start table instead, and nothing calibrates the two estimators against each other. Across three builds of the engine that mismatch priced between 8.7% and 19.2% of attempts so that being CAUGHT STEALING HELPED the batting team, carrying up to 22.6% of the total decision value. Those attempts are excluded and counted. Pricing them needs an inning-level model that predicts the boundary and the mid-inning state together, which has not been built