olate it in 24.6%.","monotone_by_construction":"the base-out state enters ONLY through its run expectancy, as a single covariate with a positive coefficient, so advancing a runner always raises the batting team's win probability. That property is what makes differencing safe and it is asserted in the tests, not assumed.","smoothing_costs_the_tails":"the model is less sharp than the raw cell means at the extremes. Bottom of the ninth tied, bases empty reads 0.6295 / 0.5868 / 0.5556 by outs against published values near 0.63 / 0.57 / 0.52: the leadoff cell matches and the two-out cell is about three points high. That is the price of a functional form smooth enough to difference, and it is a price worth paying, because a table that is right on average and non-monotone in the base state cannot value a decision at all. Any family reading the ninth-inning tail should say so.","state_excludes":"the teams, the batter, the pitcher, the park and the count. Every one matters to a real win probability and every one would let a manager's roster leak into his grade. This is a league-average valuation of a SITUATION, which is the only thing a decision can be fairly scored against."},"teams":{"status":"built","n_rows":240,"rows":[{"team":"MIA","season":2026,"attempts":103,"success_rate":0.7864,"share_2B":0.7864,"share_3B":0.2136,"mean_breakeven_faced":0.7567},{"team":"CLE","season":2026,"attempts":96,"success_rate":0.8125,"share_2B":0.8333,"share_3B":0.1667,"mean_breakeven_faced":0.756},{"team":"TBR","season":2026,"attempts":92,"success_rate":0.75,"share_2B":0.9022,"share_3B":0.0978,"mean_breakeven_faced":0.7532},{"team":"MIL","season":2026,"attempts":87,"success_rate":0.7586,"share_2B":0.8736,"share_3B":0.1264,"mean_breakeven_faced":0.753},{"team":"NYY","season":2026,"attempts":86,"success_rate":0.7558,"share_2B":0.814,"share_3B":0.186,"mean_breakeven_faced":0.7513},{"team":"WSN","season":2026,"attempts":85,"success_rate":0.8471,"share_2B":0.8118,"share_3B":0.1765,"mean_breakeven_